  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. Emily peels \\(7\\) shrimp per minute.\n2. In \\(10\\) minutes, she can peel:\n   \\[\n   7 \\times 10 = 70\n   \\]\n3. Since \\(70\\) is fewer than the \\(100\\) shrimp available, she can peel and sauté all \\(70\\) shrimp.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{70\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Emily can peel 6 shrimp per minute.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\text{ shrimp/minute} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}=60\\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nSince 60 is fewer than the 100 available, she can peel and sauté:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{60\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now let me ask about just one part of that. How many shrimp can Emily peel in ten minutes? Additionally, Emily discards 5 shrimp after peeling them because they are damaged.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nAfter discarding 5 damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n60-5=\\boxed{55\\text{ usable shrimp}}\n\\]\n\nShe still peeled \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp in total.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 12 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp. After discarding 5 damaged shrimp, \\(55\\) remain.\n\nHer sautéing rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{30}{12}=2.5\\text{ shrimp per minute}\n\\]\n\nIn 10 minutes, she can sauté:\n\n\\[\n2.5 \\times 10=25\\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nSince she has enough usable peeled shrimp, sautéing is the limiting step. Thus, she can peel and sauté:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp and discard \\(5\\), leaving \\(55\\) usable shrimp.\n\nShe can sauté \\(30\\) shrimp in \\(10\\) minutes, so sautéing limits the total:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Emily works on each shrimp sequentially:\n\n- Peeling time per shrimp:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{60}{6}=10\\text{ seconds}\n  \\]\n- Sautéing time per shrimp:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{600}{30}=20\\text{ seconds}\n  \\]\n\nThus, each shrimp takes:\n\n\\[\n10+20=30\\text{ seconds}\n\\]\n\nIn \\(10\\) minutes, or \\(600\\) seconds, she can process:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{600}{30}=20\\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nAfter discarding \\(5\\) damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n20-5=\\boxed{15\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To successfully cook \\(90\\) shrimp, Emily must peel \\(95\\), since \\(5\\) peeled shrimp are discarded.\n\n- Peeling time:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{95}{6}\\text{ minutes}=15\\text{ minutes }50\\text{ seconds}\n  \\]\n- Cooking time:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{90}{30/10}=30\\text{ minutes}\n  \\]\n\nBecause she peels and cooks sequentially, the total time is:\n\n\\[\n15\\text{ min }50\\text{ sec}+30\\text{ min}\n=\\boxed{45\\text{ minutes }50\\text{ seconds}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
